{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramEraseCornerSurjective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramEraseCornerSurjective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramAddCell"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.exists_eraseCorner_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.exists_eraseCorner_eq","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramEraseCornerSurjective.lean#L56-L64","doc":"**Corner removal is surjective.** Every Young diagram `ν` is obtained from some strictly larger\ndiagram by deleting a removable corner — take `ν` with the cell past the end of its first row\nadjoined. Together with `card_eraseCorner` this is what lets a `∀ ν` statement about diagrams of\nsize `m+1` be proved by working upstairs at `m+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_rowLen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isAddableCell_rowLen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/YoungDiagramEraseCornerSurjective.lean#L51-L54","doc":"The cell just past the end of row `0` is addable to any diagram. ","signatureChunk":0}]}